					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1387665#post-2402496</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1387665/sunnyclockwork-s-artwork-scp-cards#post-2402496</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2015 04:54:57 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>DrMorris</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2231487</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>That's a very good point that I hadn't considered before, I'd always assumed that &quot;unrelated entities&quot; meant the Scarlet King, therefore the Scarlet King was not the entity. I'll still stick to that view as my headcanon, but I retract my previous statements on the inaccuracy of the reference.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1387665#post-2402405</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1387665/sunnyclockwork-s-artwork-scp-cards#post-2402405</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2015 01:35:29 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>dankaar</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1790336</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Note that &quot;Similar, but unrelated&quot; doesn't outright say it's NOT the Scarlet King. It just states that certain refernces don't actually describe ehat it actually is. More importantly, it specifically uses the plural of &quot;entities&quot;, meaning that the specific rituals refers to a boatload of world-ending occult entities, not just one.</p> <p>Finally, nowhere does it say that it can't use the actual entity's identity as the core of the ritual, it just needs to incorporate references ftom others. And since the goal is to pull the wool over the eyes of people who know what they're dealing with, it can make more sense to use the real thing and pass off the unusual references as &quot;archaic symbols&quot; than to make up a new entity wholecloth and risk having some bright young lad or lass figuring things out and blowing the whole masquerade by screaming &quot;THIS IS ALL FAKE!&quot;</p> <p>Either way, both views of <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2317">SCP-2317</a> on whether or not it's the Scarlet King are perfectly valid.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1387665#post-2402392</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1387665/sunnyclockwork-s-artwork-scp-cards#post-2402392</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2015 01:01:45 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Agent MacLeod</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1922529</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Death of the Author applies like, super hard on this wiki. One can interpret a work any damn way they like here, and authors have actually changed their opinions of their own work based on better interpretations.</p> 
				 	]]>
